# Rust
/target

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.so
*.pyd
# MSVC debug symbols for the extension. `maturin develop` drops a 130 MB .pdb
# next to the .pyd on Windows.
*.pdb
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Web
node_modules/

# Simulation artifacts. dump.vcd is committed on purpose: it is the fixture the
# round-trip test runs against, so CI does not need a simulator installed.
*.vvp
*.vtx/
# FST dumps are simulator output like any other — except this one, which is a
# 1.2 KB fixture: the only file in the repo that exercises the FST reader, and
# CI has no simulator that writes one.
*.fst
!designs/fifo_async/dump.fst
# libfst unpacks an FST's hierarchy into a scratch file beside the dump and
# then tries to unlink it while the handle is still open — which Windows
# refuses, so a zero-byte file is left behind on every read.
*.hier_*
# Session sidecars are per-developer here; in a real project they are committed
# on purpose (P5 — layout and bookmarks are versionable).
*.session.json
# The sidecar is written atomically via a `.tmp` next to it (api/sessions.py). A
# server killed mid-save leaves one behind, and nothing can clean it up after the
# fact — so it must not be a file `git add -A` picks up.
*.session.json.tmp

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Frontend build + test output. designs/*/sim.log IS committed: the triage
# acceptance test reads it, so CI needs no simulator.
web/dist/
# Unanchored: Playwright writes these relative to its own cwd, which is not
# always `web/` — a `-g` run from the repo root left one at the top level.
test-results/

# `pytest --cov` artefacts. Not a declared dependency — it is installed when
# somebody wants to know where the holes are, which is worth doing and not
# worth committing the output of.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
web/playwright-report/
web/vite.log

# The frontend built into the Python package for shipping (`make web-build`).
# Generated, so not committed; the wheel carries it.
python/veritrace/web/
# ModelSim / xsim / Verilator working directories.
designs/*/work/
designs/*/obj_dir/
designs/*/xsim.dir/
designs/*/dump_modelsim.do
designs/*/dump_xsim.tcl
designs/*/*.wlf
designs/*/transcript

# Scratch files from interactive probing.
probe_tmp.sv

# `veritrace run`'s work directory: the build, the waveform and the log for one
# run. Generated, and rebuilt every time.
.veritrace/
# ...and the config it writes for a reference design, which the Makefile does
# not need. A real project commits its own `.veritrace.toml` on purpose. The
# root pattern matters as much as the per-design one: `run` writes the config
# beside the working directory, so running it from here leaves one that every
# later `--rtl` command finds by searching upward.
/.veritrace.toml
designs/*/.veritrace.toml

# The simulation command `run` records for `export` to quote (§13.4b). Absolute
# paths from one machine; regenerated on every run.
designs/*/sim.command
# Records which simulator artifact the reference Makefile just produced.  This
# prevents an old dump.fst from silently winning over a fresh dump.vcd (or the
# reverse) without making machine-local build state part of the repository.
designs/*/.veritrace-trace

# §13.6's regression database. A real project commits its own on purpose; the
# one written while testing the reference designs is not history worth keeping.
/regressions.duckdb

# §8.14's cached transaction tables. Written beside a store the first time an
# interface is extracted, and rebuilt from the trace whenever they are missing.
designs/*/*.vtx.txn/

# TypeScript's incremental build state.
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Scratch output from the self-check job. Those steps `tee` their reports to the
# repository root so a failing assertion can quote the text it did not find; the
# files are evidence for one run, not sources.
/checks.txt
/corr.txt
/cov.csv
/dl.txt
/dma.txt
/dmaok.txt
/fcov.txt
/holes.txt
/mem.txt
/memok.txt
/ok.txt
/perf.txt
/perf2.txt
/triage.txt
/txn.txt
/txnwhy.txt

# cocotb's build output and its runner's cache (designs/cocotb).
sim_build/
designs/cocotb/build/
designs/cocotb/dump.vcd
designs/cocotb/sim.vvp
results.xml
